 "notes": "Headline limit: red \"MiniBooNE Dump\" 2 sigma C.L. closed exclusion contour from Fig.7 (vector file figures/MB_ARGONEUT_photon_limits2sigma.pdf), extracted by crimson RGB (0.863,0.078,0.235). Paper Lagrangian L = -(1/4) g_agamma a F Ftilde matches canonical convention directly (no conversion). Beam-dump laboratory limit (not dark matter), so dm_density is null. The contour is a closed region: points trace the drawn boundary from the low-mass flat top (~2.2e-4 GeV^-1, clipped at plot left edge m=1e3 eV) down the main diagonal (min-coupling reach), around the high-mass nose (~1.7e8 eV, ~1.3e-7 GeV^-1), and up the right edge which exits the top of the plot near m~7.5e6 eV (upper coupling boundary clipped by y-axis range). ArgoNeuT curves in the same figure are sensitivity projections (3/20/100 events, no dedicated analysis) and are NOT the measured limit. The paper also reports a g_ae limit (Fig.8) in the same way; photon coupling reported here as it is presented first in Sec.IV Results. Axis calibration from centered tick labels.",
